# ''Service owners'' — thank you: 59 of the 63 services now carry a `tjenesteeier` [service owner], so both ToDo lists and the owner grouping under //Tjenester// [services] are live. Four have none: `Flow`, `Integrasjonstjenesten`, `Junta` and `Støtte og hjelp til innovasjon`. Is that intended, or should they have one?
# ''Data cleanup'' — [[Anomalier]] [anomalies] lists the problems with the affected tiddlers. Your own clean-up in September cleared four classes outright — self-tagging, bullet lists glued to the paragraph above, tiddlers tagged both `Målsetting` [objective] and `Resultat` [key result], and monthly reviews carrying a service-type tag — and merged `Ekstern Tjeneste` into `Ekstern tjeneste` [external service]. What is left is waiting on a button, not on us. Nothing runs until someone presses one; a retag never deletes; on a server each is a file write per tiddler, with no automatic undo.
#* ''Casing drift'' (section 2) — four families remain, all typing slips, and the page preselects the majority spelling: `Juni`/`juni` (211 vs 4 tiddlers), `April`/`april` (189 vs 4), `Resultat`/`resultat` (432 vs 2), `MyHealth@EU`/`Myhealth@EU` (3 vs 1).
#* ''Reviews under a retired governance tag'' (new, section 12) — 191 reviews still carry `Styring Tiltak` [governance: initiative] or the old spelling `Styring Satsning for fart` [governance: drive for speed]. For 153 of them the page shows the tag the service's tags imply today, with one table and one button per year: 48 from 2026, 56 from 2025, 49 from 2024. You agreed to the 2026 ones. Should 2024 and 2025 follow, or stay as the history they were written as? The buttons are separate so that either answer works. The other 38 cannot be placed and are only listed: they belong to the year-versioned `Tiltaket …` [the initiative …] tiddlers, which carry `Oppgaver fra HOD` [tasks from the Ministry of Health] without `Ekstern tjeneste`.
#* ''Leftover edit drafts'' (section 10) — 15, all safe to delete with one click: each is empty, or the tiddler it drafts still holds the text.
#* ''Services with no year tag'' (new, section 13) — six: `Filoverføringstjenesten ("FOT")`, `Flow`, `Junta`, `Navet`, `Sentral forskrivningsmodul` and `Testunivers`. You said you would tag them; until then the period filter cannot hide them.
#* ''Initiatives tagged straight onto `Norsk Helsenett SF`'' (section 4) — 12 tiddlers carry `Oppgaver fra HOD` or `Satsing for fart` [drive for speed] without `Ekstern tjeneste`, so they are not services and their reviews get no governance tag. Is that the intended reading of the 2024–25 history?
# ''Archiving'' — [[Arkiv]] [archive] hides prior years behind an `Arkiv` tag, reversibly, without deleting anything. Is that enough, or should old years leave the live wiki entirely (a separate read-only archive wiki)?
# ''Business-review rules'' — the ToDo list counts a review as done only if its text differs from the template and from last month's review. Is an exact comparison right, or should a review that is a near-copy be flagged too? And should `Forretningsmessig endring` [business change, i.e. severity] be required on a new review? 76% of existing reviews lack it, so we made it optional.
# ''Which services should report?'' — the ToDo lists default to the services that have filed at least one review this year: 49 of the 63 services in the wiki have for 2026. The other 14 only appear under the //Alle tjenester// [all services] toggle, so a service that has never reported is never chased. Is that the right rule, or should the list of services expected to report be maintained explicitly?
# ''Permalink base'' — is `https://tiddlywiki.plattform.nhn.no/#…` correct?
# ''Authorisation'' — when run as a server, the wiki is currently open to all readers and writers. Should it be restricted to NHN staff? If so, how? Two options are:
#* ''Auth proxy in front of the server'' - a reverse proxy on the hosting platform authenticates each user against AD (OIDC / SAML / ADFS) and passes the verified username to TiddlyWiki in a request header. The sever supports the `readers` and `writers` lists of who may read and who may save
#* ''Two deployments'' — the server for editors, and the static single-file build for everyone else, regenerated on a schedule.
# ''Deliveries with no service link'' — [[Leveranserapport]] [delivery report] groups deliveries under the service they are tagged with, and lists the ones it cannot place. For mai–august 2026 that is 12 of 75, the same number your own script reported. Looking at them, they are two different situations:
#* ''The service is one hop away'' (8 of the 12) — the delivery is tagged a `Målsetting` [objective] such as `Sektorkontakt` or `Forutsigbarhet av tjenester og funksjonalitet for leverandørene`, and that objective is itself tagged the service (`Støtte og hjelp til leverandører`, `Helsenettet.no og Medlemstjenesten`). Nothing is wrong with the tagging — the report simply does not follow the hop. Should it, or should a delivery always carry its service tag directly? If the former, we change the report and your data stays as it is.
#* ''Work that belongs to a national initiative, not a service'' (4) — the Parek and DHG deliveries are tagged `Pasientens rekvisisjoner` (`Satsning for fart` [drive for speed]) and `Tiltaket digitalt helsekort for gravide` (`Tiltak` [initiative]). Those sit on `Norsk Helsenett SF`, above the divisions, so no service owns them. Should the board report carry a section for initiatives alongside the services, or should these deliveries also be tagged the service that does the work?
#* Separately: three of these deliveries carry `Støtte og hjelp til leverandør`, singular, where the service is `Støtte og hjelp til leverandører`, plural. That tag matches nothing at all and is worth correcting whatever you decide above.
# ''Reporting period'' — the report covers a range of months within one calendar year, which is what your own script did. Do any reporting periods cross a year boundary? And can we have the output of your script for one period, so we can compare it to ours line by line rather than only by count?
# ''Backfill `period`'' — new tiddlers created through the forms are stamped with a `period` field (`2026-03` monthly, `2026` yearly). Six reviews you have created through the form carry one; nothing older does — 2275 periodic tiddlers, of which 912 are reviews. May we run a one-off pass that stamps them from their year and month tags? It makes every period filter cheaper and less dependent on tag spelling.
# ''Deployment'' — where does the wiki run once this is finished, and who updates it? Today there is a Node.js server for editing and a single-file build for reading. We can document either, but we need to know which one NHN will operate.
# ''A stray copy of [[Tjenesteeiere]] [service owners]'' — your wiki holds an ordinary tiddler called `Tjenesteeiere`, saved on 31 August: a copy of the plugin's own page as it was then. An ordinary tiddler takes precedence over the plugin's, so every later improvement to that page — the Power BI suggestions, the faster refresh — is hidden behind it. Please delete it; the plugin's current page then shows. Any plugin page gets stuck this way if it is opened in the editor and saved.
# ''Swapping the review template'' — the `mal` [template] tiddler on your wiki still has the old wording; the reworded one you sent in September is only on the test site. Before swapping it, look at section 11 of [[Anomalier]]. It lists `12 Autentisering og autorisasjon - hovedtrekk og endringer desember 2026`, an untouched copy of the old template, which would change from «Kun mal» [template only] to written the moment the template changes. Fill it in or delete it first.
# ''Tag tiddlers after the clean-up'' — three small things that are yours to tidy. `Ekstern Tjeneste` (capital T) survives as a tiddler that nothing is tagged with, and it holds the colour, while `Ekstern tjeneste` has no tiddler and so no colour. `Styring Oppgaver fra HOD` does not exist as a tiddler yet, though the review form now applies it. And the new `Satsing for fart` and `Styring Satsing for fart` tiddlers have no colour.
